When people bring up Fuslie for the homewrecker thing, I think the thing worth considering is;

She had just ended a long term relationship herself and the guy she was talking to got close with her, he vented to her about his stuff and she did with him too, they bonded over it, he told her that he was getting a divorce, so she was under the thought that he wasn't with or intending to be with his wife anymore. She still apologizes (although she shut him down eventually because she must've come to her senses or something) but regardless- it's a little different than intentionally going after a married man vs someone who told you they're actively leaving a bad marriage or something. 

Not excusing anything here, but I do think it's still worth thinking about- He specifically told her that he was actively leaving, she herself just left a long term relationship, both were single in her eyes (divorce can take a long time, for any of you who know) Regardless, still an unfortunate situation.

